    "steps": [
      "Contact Us8 - Positron V3.2 - Base PlateThis guide contains instructions for building the base plate for the Positron V3.2.",
      "Before you start to assemble, please make sure you have these parts printed.",
      "For all the M2.5 screws, please use our screwdriver included in the kit.",
      "Turn over the base plate and insert M3x8 BHCS screws through the holes as shown in the picture. Secure M3x8x7x10 standoffs into the screws.",
      "Install M2.5x3x4 heatset inserts into holes of the printed mount.",
      "3Prepare the MotorsStep 3 of 28 in this sectionPut the motor plates on top of the motors and secure with M3x6 BHCS screws.",
      "Attach the AB motor plates to the standoffs and secure with M3x8 BHCS screws.",
      "6Install the Switch PCBStep 6 of 28 in this sectionPosition the switch PCB onto the switch PCB mount and secure with M2.5x4 SHCS screws.",
      "8Install Z Drive to the Base PlateStep 7 of 28 in this sectionThe teeth of the belt should face the pulley.",
      "Turn over the base plate and secure the Z drive using M3x8 BHCS screws.",
      "Refer to the pictures for base plate wiring. All the wires except the toolhead cable, power inlet cable and power switch cable should be wired beforehad as it will be difficult after the light strips, side panels and top covers are installed.",
      "Plug the toolhead cable to the toolhead PCB as shown in the picure. We will install the PCB in later a step.",
      "Move the Jumper above the Z_Endstop pin to the left, bridging ZSTOP and SIG. Refer to Positron Team Wiki .",
      "11Position Light Bar BracketsStep 10 of 28 in this sectionInstall M2.5x3x4 heatset inserts into the hole of the rear light bar bracket.",
      "Position the light guide strips onto the light bar bracket and secure with M2.5x6 BHCS screws.",
      "Install M2.5x3x4 heatset inserts into the holes of left panels as shown in the picture.",
      "Unscrew the nut on the switch, insert the the power switch cable through the hole of the back left side panel and screw the nut back.",
      "Install M2.5x3x4 heatset inserts into the holes of the mid panels.",
      "Position left side panel to the base plate.",
      "24Install Left Upper Top CoverStep 16 of 28 in this sectionPosition the left upper top cover to the base plate and secure with BHCS screws. Use M2.5x10 BHCS screws in the holes close to the side panels (marked 2). Use an M2.5x6 BHCS screw in the hole close to the Z drive (marked 1).",
      "Put the printed left panel cornerstones on the top cover and secure with M2.5x10 BHCS screws.",
      "25 Install the IdlersStep 17 of 28 in this sectionPosition 3x6x0.5 washers and 3mm idlers onto the standoffs and secure with M3x8 wafer head screws.",
      "Position the linear rail to the standoffs and align the holes. Secure the linear rail with M3x8 SHCS screws.",
      "Install M3x6x5 heatset inserts in the top holes of the printed part.",
      "29Install the Right Side PanelsStep 20 of 28 in this sectionInstall M2.5x3x4 heatset inserts into the rear cable panel.",
      "30Install the Right Mid PanelStep 21 of 28 in this sectionPosition the right mid panel to the base plate and secure with FHCS screws. Use an M3x6 FHCS screw in the front hole (marked 1) . Use an M2.5x6 FHCS screw in the back hole (marked 2).",
      "31 Install the Right Upper Top CoverStep 22 of 28 in this sectionPut the LED diffuser cover inside the printed LED cluster retainer and position the retainer onto the cover. Apply some glue on the indicated blue area to keep them in place.",
      "32 Install the IdlersStep 23 of 28 in this sectionPut 3x6x0.5 washers and 3mm idlers onto the standoffs and secure with M3x8 wafer head screws.",
      "34Install the Y Axis Bumper PlateStep 25 of 28 in this sectionPut the front Y axis bumper plate onto the head of the top covers and secure using M2.5x10 BHCS screws",
      "38Install the Rubber FeetStep 27 of 28 in this sectionPosition the rubber feet onto the corners of the base plate, thread M4x8x0.5 washers and secure with M4x6 BHCS screws.",
      "You now have completed the assembly of the base plate."
    ],
